{
  "id": "ss.char.donut",
  "name": "Donut",
  "description": "The lucky one. Coral curls with a ring of a bun on top — a donut, sprinkles and all — one eye shut in a wink, a grin with the tongue out. The shell closed into a ring where the emitter chamber used to be, and Donut wears that as a swim ring round the middle, coral with a white stripe, because a thing that grew over its wound may as well float on it. A row of husk spines runs off the far shoulder, and in the near hand it holds three wing blades fanned like a hand of cards: Drifter membranes on bone frames, thrown to bounce from body to body. The pouch on the ring is the jelly it hoards. Same dead organ as the rest, worn as a brooch on the rim; same bobble feelers. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
  "tags": [
    "ss-char"
  ],
